Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 section 4(b))
----------------------------------------------
`index.js` is not the upstream distribution. It differs as follows, and the
same statement appears as a banner comment at the top of the file itself:

  1. It is a single self-contained ES module produced by esbuild from the
     package's TypeScript sources, rather than the upstream rollup output.
     Its bundled dependencies (three, lit, @monogrid/gainmap-js) are inlined.
  2. A temporary server-safe globals shim is prepended, and a matching
     teardown is appended. Neither is part of the upstream work. The shim
     installs stand-ins for `HTMLElement`, `document`, `customElements` and
     related globals ONLY when they are absent — i.e. never in a browser — and
     the footer deletes them again as soon as the library body has finished
     evaluating. Its sole purpose is to let the Boxel realm indexer, which
     evaluates modules outside a browser, load this module without throwing.
  3. Minification with `--legal-comments=none` strips the per-file licence
     headers of the original sources; the banner and this NOTICE carry the
     attribution in their place.

No functional change was made to model-viewer's own code.

